# L-shaped block with over-the-block teg_mode (busterm_over_the_block.feature
# scenario 5's manual companion).
#
# Geometry:
#   L-block: tall arm (0,0)-(100,400)  +  wide base (0,0)-(400,100)
#   Notch region: x=100–400, y=100–400
#   src block:    (500,150)-(600,250)
#
# The OVER logic DOES trigger here.  This header long claimed the opposite
# ("the L-shape's notch is a diagonal notch … the OVER logic never triggers",
# with TRUNK_V@x250 connecting Direct) — that described the pre-rectilinear
# generator and had gone stale: the rectilinear partial-span bridge
# (rects_are_rectilinear + the trunk crossing some but not all rects,
# topology.cpp) emits a bridge on the union bbox's outer face.  Measured on
# main @ 8a95e98e: 7 of the 18 candidates carry a bridge over L —
# TRUNK_V@x250/x400 bridge at the union RIGHT face ((400,0)-(400,400)), the
# TRUNK_H family (y125..y325) at the union TOP face ((0,400)-(400,400)).
# The @landed BDD scenario "L-shaped block …" in busterm_over_the_block.feature
# pins the same behavior.  (An old note here pointed at a "TRUNK_V@x300 …
# xfail" BDD test; no such scenario exists any more.)
#
# Honest caveat while exploring: a bridge is generation-only today — it is
# priced into the candidate's wirelength and persisted, but no downstream
# stage plans, places, audits or draws it — and on THIS shape the emitted
# bridge is itself incomplete: it lies on the union bbox's outer face, which
# never touches the rect the trunk missed (the tall arm for V trunks, the
# base for H trunks).  See docs/internal/teg_multirect_status.md §1.1 / §1.3
# / §2.2.

add_block src 500 150 600 250
add_block L rect 0 0 100 400 rect 0 0 400 100 teg_mode over

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 0
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 0

add_net clk src.tx L.rx

run_bundler STRICT
generate_topologies_for_bundle clk src L
run_planner
run_nuts

#visualize_topologies clk
visualize

